00:54:12.790 --> 00:54:15.470
- [Audience Member] Yes,
so I guess the question...

00:54:15.470 --> 00:54:19.435
I guess not exactly I guess
is the answer to that.

00:54:19.435 --> 00:54:24.435
We have in the biological
versus the cultural ideas

00:54:27.030 --> 00:54:29.230
about evolution of language.

00:54:29.230 --> 00:54:32.727
There's this gradualist
idea that we build up

00:54:32.727 --> 00:54:37.620
cultural scaffolding from
communications systems

00:54:37.620 --> 00:54:40.830
which non-linguistic like
or part linguistic like

00:54:40.830 --> 00:54:42.850
or something like that.

00:54:42.850 --> 00:54:47.850
But we also have this
biological capacity for language

00:54:48.392 --> 00:54:52.350
which is presumably relatively abrupt

00:54:52.350 --> 00:54:54.590
if it's a single gene mutation.

00:54:54.590 --> 00:54:58.280
It's the time it takes
for that to percolate

00:54:58.280 --> 00:55:02.390
through a population
which could be anything...

00:55:02.390 --> 00:55:03.223
- [Interpreter] Interpreters are actually

