00:56:41.650 --> 00:56:44.733
- [Audience Member] Mr.
Shea, in your striking book

00:56:44.733 --> 00:56:47.900
the Language of Light, one
of the more striking aspects

00:56:47.900 --> 00:56:51.210
of the story of Deaf
education to me, anyway,

00:56:51.210 --> 00:56:53.230
was the role of Helen
Keller in that story.

00:56:53.230 --> 00:56:55.180
You wanna tell a little bit about that?

00:56:58.200 --> 00:57:00.170
- The answer would be a long one

00:57:00.170 --> 00:57:02.250
but I'll try to make it short.

00:57:02.250 --> 00:57:03.600
Helen Keller was remarkable.

00:57:03.600 --> 00:57:06.940
She was Deaf and Blind
from the age of about seven

00:57:06.940 --> 00:57:09.920
and she got all the way through Radcliffe

00:57:09.920 --> 00:57:14.920
but there is disappointing
evidence in the history

00:57:15.010 --> 00:57:19.720
that at a young age, the work
that was presented as her own

00:57:19.720 --> 00:57:24.720
was in fact plagiarized by
Anne Sullivan from a book.

00:57:26.420 --> 00:57:29.003
It was a great crisis in Helen's life.

00:57:29.890 --> 00:57:34.530
The head of the Perkins
School in Boston disowned her

00:57:34.530 --> 00:57:39.450
in fact and she ultimately
recovered from that.

00:57:39.450 --> 00:57:41.050
Many people jumped to her defense.

00:57:41.050 --> 00:57:44.420
She was only a child, of course,
but there is some thought

00:57:44.420 --> 00:57:47.150
that much of her writing in later life

00:57:47.150 --> 00:57:51.030
may have been written
in large part by others.

00:57:51.030 --> 00:57:53.070
Whether it was or not, she was brilliant.

00:57:53.070 --> 00:57:56.330
She did get through Radcliffe
and accomplished a lot.

00:57:56.330 --> 00:57:59.530
But one of the problems
I think Helen always had,

00:57:59.530 --> 00:58:03.290
she never learned how
to speak well audibly.

00:58:03.290 --> 00:58:05.700
She never learned how to read lips

00:58:05.700 --> 00:58:08.743
whether read lips by touch.

00:58:09.630 --> 00:58:14.630
But Alexander Graham Bell used
her as a kind of adversement

00:58:14.830 --> 00:58:19.820
for Oralist teaching and
his favorite phrase well

00:58:19.820 --> 00:58:24.820
if Blind and Deaf Helen
Keller can speak and read lips

00:58:25.174 --> 00:58:28.560
and learn so much then why can't the Deaf

00:58:28.560 --> 00:58:31.030
or not Blind accomplish that?

00:58:31.030 --> 00:58:34.980
But lots of what he said
about Helen was false.

00:58:34.980 --> 00:58:38.960
It also turns out in history
that when Helen was very young

00:58:39.830 --> 00:58:43.080
she had a well developed
system of home signs

00:58:43.080 --> 00:58:45.670
which could have been
with the proper teachers

00:58:45.670 --> 00:58:48.760
or somebody like Bébian and his successors

00:58:48.760 --> 00:58:53.760
turned her into an even more
remarkable woman, a genius,

00:58:56.370 --> 00:59:01.370
than she was without
the ability to practice

00:59:02.470 --> 00:59:04.270
her own native language.

00:59:04.270 --> 00:59:06.310
Those who are interested,
there's a full chapter

00:59:06.310 --> 00:59:08.280
on Helen in the Language
of Light and you all

00:59:08.280 --> 00:59:10.320
may find it interesting.

00:59:10.320 --> 00:59:11.153
Thank you.

00:59:17.020 --> 00:59:17.853
- Okay, sure.

