01:00:17.970 --> 01:00:19.650
So it seems like if you're missing

01:00:19.650 --> 01:00:22.590
your fundamental language,
a foundational language,

01:00:22.590 --> 01:00:25.070
you're really at a disadvantage.

01:00:25.070 --> 01:00:27.400
Also, with us, you know,
with hearing parents

01:00:27.400 --> 01:00:29.550
we're always talking to
our child so right away,

01:00:29.550 --> 01:00:32.640
you know, it's putting on
the jacket, the booties.

01:00:32.640 --> 01:00:34.070
This is milk.

01:00:34.070 --> 01:00:36.370
You know, we're constantly
making a connection to things

01:00:36.370 --> 01:00:38.930
for them to be able to,
you know, gain knowledge

01:00:38.930 --> 01:00:39.920
of their environment.

01:00:39.920 --> 01:00:42.020
I was just curious when
you were in Nicaragua,

01:00:42.020 --> 01:00:44.680
did you find any Deaf
parents with Deaf children,

01:00:44.680 --> 01:00:48.800
or did you find families
