01:00:48.800 --> 01:00:50.740
to be able to see how they communicated

01:00:50.740 --> 01:00:52.610
and if that communication
was so much better

01:00:52.610 --> 01:00:55.110
because their children
were getting right away

01:00:55.110 --> 01:00:56.948
connections to the environment rather than

01:00:56.948 --> 01:01:00.270
three years of delayed
nothing, no language,

01:01:00.270 --> 01:01:02.460
no fundamental language
until they got into school.

01:01:02.460 --> 01:01:04.170
Did you find any families like that

01:01:04.170 --> 01:01:06.370
or is that something
you'd be interested in?

01:01:08.130 --> 01:01:08.963
Thank you.

01:01:11.750 --> 01:01:15.530
- [Interpreter] There
are a few individuals

01:01:15.530 --> 01:01:20.530
who have Deaf relatives,
Deaf aunts, and so forth.

01:01:21.330 --> 01:01:25.810
Yes, their language tends to be

01:01:27.270 --> 01:01:29.540
on par with what we would see

01:01:29.540 --> 01:01:32.123
in a typically developing situation.

01:01:33.890 --> 01:01:37.420
Absolutely having a rich environment

01:01:37.420 --> 01:01:40.450
has a positive impact on
their language development.

01:01:40.450 --> 01:01:42.540
One thing I want to make
sure that I emphasize,

01:01:42.540 --> 01:01:46.384
so often hearing parents
who have a Deaf child

01:01:46.384 --> 01:01:50.030
are afraid, how will I learn
Sign Language well enough?

01:01:50.030 --> 01:01:51.030
I can't possibly do that.

01:01:51.030 --> 01:01:52.730
That's not my language.

01:01:52.730 --> 01:01:55.390
That fear sometimes drives them,

01:01:55.390 --> 01:01:57.750
and there are a multitude
of other reasons as well,

01:01:57.750 --> 01:02:00.033
drive them to using spoken English.

01:02:04.198 --> 01:02:07.150
I didn't highlight this
in my talk but a lot

01:02:07.150 --> 01:02:09.180
of what we know is that children

01:02:09.180 --> 01:02:13.020
are prodigious language learners

01:02:13.020 --> 01:02:17.663
and they often will surpass their input.

01:02:19.190 --> 01:02:22.880
Really, the message that
we want to send to parents

01:02:22.880 --> 01:02:25.373
is that anything helps.

01:02:26.980 --> 01:02:29.750
Learning sign with your kid helps

01:02:29.750 --> 01:02:32.543
their language development,
that's been shown.

01:02:34.880 --> 01:02:38.620
So don't underestimate what the kid has

01:02:38.620 --> 01:02:39.883
and what they can do.

01:02:43.430 --> 01:02:45.090
- [Interpreter] Right.

01:02:45.090 --> 01:02:48.240
And Deaf families in
Nicaragua are quite rare.

01:02:48.240 --> 01:02:51.810
I actually don't know
anyone whose taken a look

01:02:51.810 --> 01:02:52.890
at counting that.

01:02:52.890 --> 01:02:56.240
We know of a few but there aren't many.

01:02:56.240 --> 01:02:59.290
I feel like there's more
here in the United States,

01:02:59.290 --> 01:03:00.760
but I could be wrong.

01:03:00.760 --> 01:03:03.010
I don't think there's
ever been a count done.

01:03:05.300 --> 01:03:08.070
In Nicaragua, I certainly
don't know of many

01:03:08.070 --> 01:03:09.623
but a couple, yes.

01:03:13.710 --> 01:03:15.210
- [Woman] Okay, last question.

01:03:17.350 --> 01:03:18.590
- [Audience Member] I
already spoke so I'm happy

01:03:18.590 --> 01:03:20.690
to give up the mic to somebody who hasn't.

01:03:38.180 --> 01:03:39.450
- [Woman] Why don't you
speak so the interpreters

01:03:39.450 --> 01:03:40.283
can hear you?

01:03:40.283 --> 01:03:42.330
- [Audience Member] Okay, I'll just talk.

01:03:42.330 --> 01:03:44.290
So I have a couple questions.

01:03:44.290 --> 01:03:49.290
My first one being as two
highly successful Deaf women,

01:03:51.130 --> 01:03:54.070
how do you go about facing
prejudice in the work place?

01:03:54.070 --> 01:03:56.070
I mean, that's just
really fascinating to me.

01:03:56.070 --> 01:03:59.280
I'm a coder and so I
kind of have experience

01:03:59.280 --> 01:04:00.310
seeing that prejudice.

01:04:00.310 --> 01:04:01.430
I'm just wondering...

01:04:01.430 --> 01:04:04.890
I mean, I'm so, so happy
that you guys are here.

01:04:04.890 --> 01:04:06.043
I don't know.

01:04:06.043 --> 01:04:07.003
I'm just interested in that.

01:04:08.500 --> 01:04:10.730
How do you give advice
about counteracting that

01:04:10.730 --> 01:04:12.280
prejudice and thinks like that?

01:04:15.332 --> 01:04:17.931
Sorry, that's so much.

01:04:17.931 --> 01:04:19.140
(audience laughing)

01:04:19.140 --> 01:04:20.140
- [Interpreter] Wow.

01:04:28.550 --> 01:04:33.550
Yes, it's okay in many
different ways, all the time.

01:04:37.419 --> 01:04:40.169
- [Audience Member] I'm so sorry.

01:04:42.228 --> 01:04:44.290
- [Interpreter] Maybe it will be helpful

01:04:44.290 --> 01:04:47.100
if you are curious about
if we're currently facing

01:04:47.100 --> 01:04:50.580
that prejudice as adults
or when we were younger

01:04:50.580 --> 01:04:53.457
because my answer would be
different in those two contexts.

01:04:53.457 --> 01:04:55.734
- [Audience Members] You
guys are both working at

01:04:55.734 --> 01:04:57.540
high ranking institutions.

01:04:57.540 --> 01:04:59.590
Do you feel like you
still experience that?

01:04:59.590 --> 01:05:00.423
Okay.

01:05:02.310 --> 01:05:03.823
Sorry, that's a bad question.

01:05:06.080 --> 01:05:07.380
- [Interpreter] It's fine.

01:05:09.710 --> 01:05:14.710
- [Interpreter] Okay, yes, I
can say a couple of things.

01:05:15.870 --> 01:05:19.603
Yes, I do experience things like that.

01:05:24.760 --> 01:05:29.760
Also, I have created a space for myself

01:05:31.670 --> 01:05:34.240
at my current place of employment

01:05:34.240 --> 01:05:38.500
where I make it work for me.

01:05:38.500 --> 01:05:41.953
I make it that way
intentionally for myself.

01:05:44.770 --> 01:05:48.730
And also I have support from colleagues

01:05:48.730 --> 01:05:49.923
in my workplace.

01:05:52.200 --> 01:05:57.120
So to be honest, I think
I have a pretty good place

01:05:57.120 --> 01:06:00.910
of employment where my
colleagues are supportive of me

01:06:00.910 --> 01:06:04.810
and my work and they listen
to what I have to say

01:06:04.810 --> 01:06:05.733
about what I need.

01:06:08.030 --> 01:06:12.580
They basically allow me
to design the system there

01:06:13.430 --> 01:06:15.980
that I want, that works for me.

01:06:15.980 --> 01:06:20.093
I think it's partly because,
well, quite honestly

01:06:22.120 --> 01:06:24.010
I don't know why that is.

01:06:24.010 --> 01:06:26.563
I do feel that there are
just good people there.

01:06:28.650 --> 01:06:31.340
- [Interpreter] Just, I'll
briefly add one thing.

01:06:31.340 --> 01:06:33.650
This goes back to the intro of this panel.

01:06:33.650 --> 01:06:36.340
I'm lucky that I'm in
the field that I'm in

01:06:36.340 --> 01:06:39.160
that appreciates the
importance of Sign Language,

01:06:39.160 --> 01:06:41.470
not only socially but on an intellectual

01:06:41.470 --> 01:06:43.640
and academic level.

01:06:43.640 --> 01:06:45.932
I'm also lucky because my institution

01:06:45.932 --> 01:06:50.830
has a lot of resources to
support me in that work

01:06:50.830 --> 01:06:55.700
but being in an environment where people

01:06:55.700 --> 01:06:59.650
really are appreciative of
the study of Sign Language

01:06:59.650 --> 01:07:02.583
like you all are, that helps a lot.

01:07:08.250 --> 01:07:11.210
That's why I really
thank you all for hosting

01:07:11.210 --> 01:07:13.029
this wonderful event.

01:07:13.029 --> 01:07:14.380
Thank you.
- Thank you.

01:07:14.380 --> 01:07:16.164
Thank you very much.

01:07:16.164 --> 01:07:19.164
(audience applauds)

01:07:20.582 --> 01:07:23.415
(whimsical music)

